WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.370
Monkey D. Luffy is officially a Yonkou.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:10.929
Gear 5 has turned him into one of the strongest
characters in the series - but his crew has

00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:14.900
become powerful right along side him.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.190
It begs the question: could any of the Straw
Hats actually beat their captain in a fight?

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:25.769
And if they couldn’t take down Luffy individually,
could they manage it if they all teamed up?

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:29.259
The first crew member we have for Luffy to
fight is Jinbe.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:34.309
As we know from Madame Sharley’s fortune
telling predictions, Luffy is destined to

00:00:34.309 --> 00:00:36.520
destroy Fishman Island one day.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.809
While that probably means the Fishmen will
be returning to the surface, let’s say that,

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:45.510
for the sake argument, Jinbe isn’t going
to like Luffy demolishing his home town.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.880
For this reason, Jinbe will fight Luffy.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:56.170
Jinbe, I think, has the best chance of defeating
Luffy of anybody in the Straw Hat crew.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.800
His specialty is fighting underwater.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.199
Luffy cannot move underwater.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:05.960
If Jinbe can use his Fishman Karate to get
Luffy off the ship and into the ocean, he

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.960
wins.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.299
The last time Luffy was submerged, he used
the Voice of all Things to call for help from

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:15.670
Law’s crew and their submarine, but we’re
going to assume there are no submarines running

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.900
interference in this fight.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:24.790
If the fight is happening on land, Jinbe loses
for certain.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:30.979
Even though he’s a former Shichibukai, he
just doesn’t have the same immense strength

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:33.040
that his yonkou captain has.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.510
As a disciplined fighter, he’d give Luffy
an excellent fight, but he just wouldn’t

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.460
be able to take it all the way.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.630
Brook has an excellent reason to want to face
off against Luffy.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.969
Two, in fact.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:48.299
Firstly, Luffy punched his best friend Laboon
right in the face.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:53.690
If he ever found out, he’d be in the right
to give Luffy a taste of his own medicine.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:02:00.250
Secondly, Luffy’s just an awful singer (Sorry
to everyone who loves the captain’s musical

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.250
stylings).

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.970
Brook’s strength among the crew is definitely
underrated.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:10.069
He was the first crew member to wound a yonkou…or
at least her homie.

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:15.110
It’s easy to forget he’s strong on account
that he’s never really had a featured fight

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.700
in the series (we’re not going to count
his opponent on Fishman Island, whom he defeated

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.849
with ease).

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:26.530
He’d fare especially well against Luffy
considering that he’s a sword wielder and

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.390
cutting attacks are Luffy’s weakness.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.430
He can also run on top of the water, while
Luffy can’t swim, so a battle taking place

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.120
on the ocean might be to Brook’s benefit.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.790
In addition, he could distract Luffy with
certified bangers if he brings his guitar

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:42.790
to the fight.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.150
However, this is Luffy we’re talking about.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.560
He’s unbelievably strong and would probably
break all of Brook’s bones…which is all

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.620
of him.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.620
Yohohoho.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.840
It’s only a matter of time until one day
Luffy hogs all of the cola on the ship and

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.790
drinks it without asking.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:04.200
After that Franky is going to be real mad
and will take his revenge on the sugary soda

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.310
thief.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:10.090
Cyborg Franky has one of the best chances
out of the crew to be able to take out Luffy.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.760
It’s not because he’s as strong as some
other crewmates.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:19.200
More so it’s just because he has the shiniest
objects to distract Luffy with.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.520
Franky has a giant mech suit, the Franky Shogun.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:29.500
And every single time Franky pilots this mech,
Luffy loses his mind with absolute wonder

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.180
and amazement.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.390
Even Franky’s nipple lights turn make Luffy’s
eyes turn to stars as he hoots and hollers

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.230
at the mechanical marvels.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:42.610
Can Luffy bring himself to destroy something
that he finds so beautiful?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:48.670
Well, yes, probably - because Luffy is a destructive,
chaotic force of nature that will break everything

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.150
in his path.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:55.970
Good thing Franky is just as good at fixing
stuff as he is at building stuff.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.430
Up next is Nico Robin.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:02.129
We’ll say that someday once Luffy finally
takes his war to the World Government, he’ll

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:04.530
want to smash up Mariejois and the Red Line.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:09.150
However, Nico Robin would reallllly like him
to preserve a lot of the historical structures

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:14.239
there, so she has to punish him for crimes
against archaeology.

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:18.590
On the surface, Robin has a better shot than
most straw hats just because she’s one of

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.729
the smartest members of the crew.

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:28.120
The problem is that she just doesn’t have
enough raw strength to deal with Luffy.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:33.610
Her fruit is geared toward more strategic
fighting, which is great to go up against

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.160
the not-so-bright Luffy.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:39.419
However, her most dependable technique is
going to be useless.

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:44.889
Sure, she could sprout arms on him to put
him in a hold, but she’s not going to be

00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:51.430
able to use “clutch” to break his neck
because his neck is made of rubber - it’ll

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.030
bend with no problem at all.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:58.900
It’s hard to imagine the sweet and kind
mascot of the crew, Chopper, ever turning

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.009
against his own.

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:03.610
So, in his scenario, it’s not going to be
about him attacking Luffy.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.699
Chopper would only fight Luffy in self-defense.

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:11.580
The Thousand Sunny has been adrift for days.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.370
The log pose is lost.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:18.120
Even Nami can’t figure out how to navigate
the ship to safety.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.240
Their food is completely depleted.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:25.960
Well, almost all their food: all that remains
is the Straw Hats’ emergency food supply.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.960
Otherwise known as Tony-Tony Chopper.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:34.169
With Chopper’s ultimate form, Monster point,
only being enough to hold off Queen until

00:05:34.169 --> 00:05:40.490
Sanji arrived on the scene, he’s not going
to have nowhere near enough raw power to compete

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.490
with Luffy.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:46.340
However, there’s one technique that we haven’t
seen in a long time that might be able to

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:51.860
help Chopper somewhat: Brain Point.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:57.610
Using his brain point transformation, Chopper
can identify the weaknesses of his opponents

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.470
and then hopefully take advantage of them.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:08.090
However, with Luffy being as strong as he
is, it’s unclear what exactly his weakness

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:12.960
would be that Chopper could exploit.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.710
One final way that Chopper might be able to
win is by utilizing his rumble balls - not

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.970
by Chopper eating them himself, though.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:24.030
Instead, Chopper might be able to convince
Luffy to try them out by convincing him that

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.030
they’re candy.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.680
Now that we know that Luffy is technically
a mythical zoan, by feeding him several rumble

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.400
balls, Chopper might be able to force some
unconventional transformations.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.340
If he can get Luffy to turn monster point,
the other crew members might have to stop

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:44.310
him from rampaging and destroying the ship,
which could in turn give Chopper enough time

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.900
to escape and avoid becoming dinner.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.729
Up next to face Luffy is none other than Nami
the Cat Burglar.

00:06:51.729 --> 00:06:56.520
In this fictional scenario, she’ll be unable
to resist the huge amount of berries on Luffy’s

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.520
head.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.200
Sadly for the greediest of the Straw Hats,
though, there’s another thing she’ll be

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.740
unable to do, and that’s harm Luffy in any
way.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:10.169
There are, of course, plenty of gags where
Oda has Nami let loose an effective punch

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:14.539
on her stronger counterparts, but that’s
all it is - a gag.

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:19.960
If it comes down to a serious fight, Nami’s
best weapon is always to use her Clima-Tact

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.310
and Zeus to bring lightning down on an opponent.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:27.220
And as we learned from Luffy’s fight with
Enel…that’s not gonna work.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:32.180
In fact, now that he has the ludicrous powers
of Gear 5, he’ll just be able to grab the

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.009
lightning and throw it right back.

00:07:35.009 --> 00:07:39.699
Sorry Nami, you’re not expanding your bank
account with this one.

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:44.419
Usopp is a Straw Hat that we’ve actually
already seen fight Luffy.

00:07:44.419 --> 00:07:49.840
In one of the greatest fights in the entire
series, they went head to head in Water 7

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.009
over the ownership of the Going Merry.

00:07:52.009 --> 00:07:57.840
After all of that, it would be very unlikely
for Usopp to ever want to face his captain

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:58.840
again.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.639
For the sake of argument, though, let’s
say that while they’re approaching Laugh

00:08:00.639 --> 00:08:06.949
Tale, Usopp contracts a terrible case of “can’t
go to that island” disease that he caught

00:08:06.949 --> 00:08:07.949
from Buggy.

00:08:07.949 --> 00:08:11.960
In fact, he doesn’t want to go to Laugh
Tale so badly that he’s going to fight his

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:14.490
captain to prevent this from happening.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.569
Sadly, though, this is probably going to play
out just like it did on Water 7.

00:08:19.569 --> 00:08:24.840
In fact, things will be even worse for Usopp
because no matter how many Pop Greens he has

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:32.029
now, they’re not going to compete with any
of Luffy’s Gears or any of the three types

00:08:32.029 --> 00:08:35.800
of haki.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:41.729
To give Usopp any kind of a chance, he’s
going to have to need a whole lot of prep

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:42.729
time.

00:08:42.729 --> 00:08:46.540
Since he has tapped into observation haki,
he’s going to have to use that paired with

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.480
his incredible sniper skills if he wants a
hope in hell.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.870
So we’re going to say that he’s found
a nice bunch of seastone bullets to put in

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:59.510
his slingshot and in addition, he’s going
to want to fight Luffy from another island

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.450
a few kilometers away.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:06.310
If he can get lucky, he might just be able
to shoot Luffy into the ocean with a well-placed

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.770
shot, but…I’m still going to give Luffy
the advantage even with those handicaps in

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:13.230
place.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:18.940
Sanji is yet another Straw Hat who has already
had a matchup against Luffy.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.649
And he actually won!

00:09:21.649 --> 00:09:27.260
The catch is…Luffy refused to fight back
whatsoever.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:30.010
Something tells me this isn’t going to go
as well this time.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:34.360
Now that Big Mom isn’t threatening the crew,
though - and moreover, Luffy’s an emperor

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.960
himself, what would make Sanji want to fight
Luffy in the first place?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.440
Eh, let’s just say Luffy hit a girl.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.800
Or, in a very uncharacteristic move, he didn’t
finish his plate.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:52.610
No matter how you slice it…er, kick it…this
is gonna be a tough one for Sanji.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:57.100
Even with his Germa power-ups, Luffy is far
stronger.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.079
Sanji is potentially faster than Luffy, since
he can move too fast to even be perceived

00:10:02.079 --> 00:10:03.079
by opponents.

00:10:03.079 --> 00:10:07.560
However, that speed won’t help much when
going up against both Luffy’s durability

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.910
and future sight.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:13.579
There’s only one thing Sanji’s going to
be able to do to even the playing field.

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:18.880
He’s going to have to feed Luffy and distract
him with delicious meat.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:24.200
I’d say Sanji could poison Luffy this way,
but as we saw in Whole Cake Island, using

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:27.829
poisons would go against everything Sanji
stands for.

00:10:27.829 --> 00:10:32.780
And even if he did, Luffy has incredible poison
tolerance.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:40.149
Nope - the only thing Sanji can do is to cook
a meal so satisfying that it renders Luffy

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:41.370
unconscious.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:46.680
Wait a second…does this mean that Sanji
actually has the best chance against Luffy

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.680
so far?

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:52.880
I guess the only question is, can Sanji cook
a meal large enough to satisfy Luffy’s immense

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.320
hunger?

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:02.940
We have only one Straw Hat left for Luffy
to face down against.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:07.550
Imagine it: the crew is hanging out on Laugh
Tale, having finally made it to the end of

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:11.519
the Grand Line…when suddenly, Luffy hears
it:

00:11:11.519 --> 00:11:17.930
“Santoryu” - It’s Pirate Hunter Zoro,
finished with the biggest long con in manga

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:24.290
history, and he’s ready to claim the Luffy’s
massive bounty.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:30.630
Now, obviously, this wouldn’t *actually*
happen - Zoro is the most loyal guy in fiction,

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:34.510
but we’re going to have fun today seeing
exactly what it would take to bring all of

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.899
the Straw Hats into conflict with Luffy and
look at how each of those fights would play

00:11:38.899 --> 00:11:39.899
out.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:45.459
Zoro and Luffy actually fought once before,
all the way back at Whiskey Peak.

00:11:45.459 --> 00:11:51.639
Oda-Sensei’s editors urged that he bring
the two in conflict to bring more excitement

00:11:51.639 --> 00:11:57.360
into the story and what resulted was a wildly
out of character moment for Luffy that a lot

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.370
of fans hate to this day.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:04.010
However, these two have grown a whole lot
since the beginning of the Grand Line, so

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:08.110
how would it play out at the end of the series?

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:14.529
Zoro probably has the best chance out of any
of the other Straw Hats for two reasons.

00:12:14.529 --> 00:12:19.410
First, because he’s a straight up beast
- just like Luffy he has access to all three

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.410
types of haki.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:26.230
But secondly, it’s because his specialty
is Luffy’s biggest weakness: blades.

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:31.780
Luffy’s rubber body can endure all sorts
of blunt objects, brute force, even bullets

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:36.730
and cannonballs - but he’s susceptible to
being cut.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:42.529
There’s no telling whose armament haki would
win out - would Luffy be able to block a sword

00:12:42.529 --> 00:12:47.890
as powerful as Enma with his haki-coated fist?

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:52.450
One advantage that Luffy does have, though,
is his future sight observation haki.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:57.260
He’s actually theorized to have tapped into
this power all the way back during Marineford

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:01.810
when he dodged one of Mihawk’s slashes and
saved his arms from being cut clean off.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:07.130
If Luffy was able to dodge a slice from Zoro’s
mentor all the way back before he properly

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:15.350
trained his haki abilities, he should be able
to avoid most of Zoro’s attacks now, too.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:24.620
And even a transformation like Asura can’t
save Zoro from the chaotic power that is Gear

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.620
5.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:29.990
Roronoa Zoro is a pretty serious, no-nonsense
guy.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:35.399
One Luffy tapped into the Toon Force, I don’t
think Zoro would be able to handle the absolute

00:13:35.399 --> 00:13:37.920
goofiest form of Luffy.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:42.769
If anything he’d get so frustrated by Luffy
not taking the fight seriously that he’d

00:13:42.769 --> 00:13:46.940
lose his cool and allow Luffy to catch him
off his guard.

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:54.639
It would be super hard for any of the Straw
Hats to beat Luffy individually - after all,

00:13:54.639 --> 00:13:56.889
he’s the captain for a reason.

00:13:56.889 --> 00:14:03.149
But what if it came down to everyone working
together to take him down?

00:14:03.149 --> 00:14:08.240
One of the best team ups in One Piece came
when the whole crew banded together to fight

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:14.200
Oars, who ironically had Luffy’s shadow,
but what if they didn’t fight his shadow?

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.940
What if the crew worked together to fight
the real thing?

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:22.070
To start the battle, we have Nami, Usopp,
and Chopper…running away.

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:27.449
For Usopp, this is tactical - his sniping
skills are at their strongest when he can

00:14:27.449 --> 00:14:30.779
create distance between him and his opponent…Ah,
who am I kidding?

00:14:30.779 --> 00:14:35.949
They’re all super scared to fight Luffy,
so they go to hide behind a big boulder while

00:14:35.949 --> 00:14:39.500
the rest of the crew starts out the fight.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:46.019
Doing the opposite and launching into action
are Sanji and Zoro.

00:14:46.019 --> 00:14:50.380
However, before they arrive at Luffy, they
crash into each other.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.199
Refusing to let the other be the first one
to land a hit on their captain, they break

00:14:54.199 --> 00:15:00.400
off into a battle of their own, while hurling
insults at one another.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:05.720
Therefore, that leaves the more reasonable
and mature members of the crew to start off

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:11.820
the fight: And in a complete act of maturity,
Brook starts jamming out on guitar while Franky

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.500
lets his nipple lights shine.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.560
Gear 5 Luffy already can’t stop laughing,
so his crewmates’ entertaining antics make

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.589
him go nuts.

00:15:21.589 --> 00:15:25.170
Nico Robin uses this opportunity to use Mil
Fleurs to grab onto Luffy’s limbs and tie

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:28.650
him down to the ground, immobilizing him.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:35.449
This barely registers for Luffy, who’s still
laughing uncontrollably at Franky and Brook.

00:15:35.449 --> 00:15:41.870
Jinbei takes this opening to use a Fishman
Karate technique, striking Luffy with a huge

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.329
surge of water.

00:15:43.329 --> 00:15:49.110
The now wet Luffy, though, is ready to take
things seriously…at least as seriously as

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.810
Gear 5 Luffy can get.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:55.899
Using his Toon Force, he spins around like
the Tasmanian Devil, twisting up Robin’s

00:15:55.899 --> 00:15:58.680
arms and freeing himself in the process.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:02.620
Robin’s strength just isn’t enough to
hold him down.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:06.540
He spins himself dry and in the process runs
right over the Fishman.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:12.680
Franky tries a radical beam, but he swallows
it right up just like he does with Kizaru’s

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:16.380
on Egghead Island and he just gets a bad case
of heartburn.

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:21.519
Brook tries to take him out with a sword technique,
but before he can, the ground becomes a whole

00:16:21.519 --> 00:16:26.100
lot bouncier than before, and Brook is sent
flying…right into the boulder that the Weakling

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.930
Trio is hiding behind.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:31.260
After plenty of screaming, it’s their chance
to try.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:35.589
Chopper transforms into Monster Point and
attempts to hold Luffy down, giving the others

00:16:35.589 --> 00:16:36.730
a chance to escape.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:43.110
Meanwhile, Usopp readies his shot: a crazy
spicy tobasco star right into Luffy’s mouth.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:50.690
Unfortunately, Gear 5 Luffy can already swallow
lasers, so a little hot sauce is nothing.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:55.800
However, the fire that shoots out of Luffy’s
mouth does singe Chopper’s beautiful coat

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.130
of fur and takes out the reindeer.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:03.310
In a last ditch effort, Nami unleashes her
most powerful attack, courtesy of Zeus…Of

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:08.250
course, fear has overridden her logical thinking,
and the lightning strike does nothing to Luffy’s

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.319
rubber body.

00:17:09.319 --> 00:17:16.020
She tries to ride Zeus away to safety while
Luffy punches Usopp into the stratosphere…unfortunately

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:20.890
knocking right into Nami, making them blast
off again Team Rocket Style.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:28.069
Luffy laughs at their misfortune, when suddenly
a flaming leg strikes him on top of the head,

00:17:28.069 --> 00:17:30.910
pounding him like a nail into the ground.

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:35.660
Sanji was the faster of the two pirate king’s
wings, after all.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:39.130
Zoro runs in after, ready to slice Luffy.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:44.930
Unfortunately, before he can, the ground breaks
apart, and both Zoro and Sanji fall into the

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.360
chasm where they find a Giant Gear 5 Luffy.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:54.720
Zoro slashes at the giant’s legs, but thanks
to Luffy’s armament haki, they’re just

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:55.720
minor cuts.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:18:00.690
Meanwhile Sanji uses his Sky Walk to try and
kick at Luffy’s head, but both the swordsman

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:04.520
and the cook are quickly scooped up into Luffy’s
clutches.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.720
Holding them there, Luffy laughs proclaiming
his victory against his crew and wishing them

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.460
better luck in their next training exercise.

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:18.410
It’s no surprise that Luffy would take the
W against his crew mates.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:25.789
After all, Zoro could only scratch Kaidou
while Gear 5 Luffy finally took down the Yonkou.

00:18:25.789 --> 00:18:30.980
However, as the crew gets stronger and stronger,
it makes you wonder whether Zoro will be strong

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:35.630
enough to take down someone like Kaidou on
his own.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:41.730
Luckily, we answered that very question in
this video: “What if Zoro fought all of

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:46.179
Luffy’s Opponents”?

